== 4. Next step ================================================ 
  Read section 1 and answer two questions: 
 
    (a) Is there per-spot ANNOTATION in the deposit (nevus vs 
        melanoma, or cluster/topic labels)? If yes, we use their 
        classification and the analysis is a paired comparison of 
        RASSF9 between annotated compartments within each patient. 
        If no, we derive spot classes from melanocytic markers plus 
        PRAME, which their paper reports as negative in the nevus 
        component and positive in the melanoma component in all 18 
        cases -- a weaker assignment, and it must be validated 
        before any RASSF9 number is read off it. 
 
    (b) How large is the download, and are the matrices per sample 
        or one combined file? That decides whether we pull all 18 
        samples or start with two or three. 
 
